   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the multiple dwelling law, in relation to requiring the\ninspection of non-fireproof buildings and compliance with the New York\nproperty maintenance code",
    "basePrintNo": "S6089",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6089-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 23,
       "fullName": "Diane J. Savino",
       "imgName": "403_diane_j._savino.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 403,
       "sessionMemberId": 1835,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "SAVINO"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §140-a, Mult Dwell L",
    "lawSection": "Multiple Dwelling Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6089\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the multiple dwelling law, in relation to requiring the\ninspection of non-fireproof buildings and compliance with the New York\nproperty maintenance code\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to ensure that tenants live in safe\nand habitable conditions and that repairs to the properties they live in\nare completed in a timely fashion.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new Section 140-A to the Multiple Dwelling Law that\nrequires all non-fireproof buildings to be inspected every 3 years and\nto be compliant with the Property Maintenance Code of New York State\n(PMCNYS) within 6 months of inspection. All landlords that do not make\nthe necessary repairs or improvements to become compliant with the\nPMCNYS will be fined $100 per day until the building becomes compliant.\nAny buildings that are non-compliant with the PMCNYS for 6 months or\nmore shall have a lien placed on the property until all repairs or\nimprovements are completed and rents adjusted based on rent abatements\ndue to the unsafe conditions originating from the non-compliance.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOn January 6, 2021, a terrible fire occurred in Inwood resulting in the\ndisplacement of 23 families. Landlords have affirmative obligations to\nensure that their property is compliant with applicable laws and regu-\nlations and that any repairs needed are done in a timely manner. Tenants\nshould have the peace of mind that their homes are safe to live in and\nshould not have to worry that an electrical fire might upend their\nlives. New York is full of residential properties that are filled with\nantiquated electrical circuits. It is imperative that landlords of these\nproperties take the necessary steps to ensure the electric circuits in\ntheir tenant's homes are safe and compliant with the National Electrical\nCode that is currently approved by the State of New York and the rele-\nvant locality. This legislation will ensure that landlords are compliant\nwith PMCNYS otherwise they will receive a monetary penalty for failing\nto do so.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nSTATE AND LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
